{"id":"p06-l01","minutes":30,"summary":"Every sensor register is a pattern of bits, and reading it wrong gives garbage. You derive positional notation and two’s complement, negate by “invert and add one”, detect overflow, and write encode/decode functions that round-trip every 16-bit value.","html":"<h2 id=\"positional-notation\">Positional notation</h2>\n<p>A number in base <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span></span></span></span> with digits <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9028em;vertical-align:-0.2083em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> means <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.1488em;vertical-align:-0.2997em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">∑</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1864em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2997em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. In binary each digit is a <strong>bit</strong>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">101</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">11</span></span></span></span>. Hexadecimal groups four bits per digit (0–9, A–F), so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">xB</span></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1011</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">010</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">181</span></span></span></span>. Datasheets write register values in hex because each hex digit maps to exactly four bits.</p>\n<p>An <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>-bit <strong>unsigned</strong> value covers <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7477em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>: 0–255 for 8 bits, 0–65 535 for 16.</p>\n<h2 id=\"two-s-complement\">Two’s complement</h2>\n<p>Signed values on every modern processor use two’s complement. The top bit (MSB) has weight <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> instead of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">+</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0724em;vertical-align:-0.2083em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:3.1032em;vertical-align:-1.3021em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.8011em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8479em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">=</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.3em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3021em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>So 8 bits cover −128 to +127, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1111</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">111</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">128</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">127</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Negation is “invert all bits, then add 1”.</strong> Inverting gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span></span></span></span>, and adding one gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7477em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span></span></span></span>, which is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span></span></span></span> modulo <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. The same adder hardware therefore handles signed and unsigned numbers: only the interpretation differs.</p>\n<p><strong>Sign extension.</strong> To widen a signed value, copy its MSB into the new upper bits: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span> in 8 bits is 0xFD, and in 16 bits 0xFFFD.</p>\n<p><strong>Overflow.</strong> Adding two signed numbers overflows when both operands have the same sign and the result has the other sign; <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span></span></span></span> in 8 bits gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">56</span></span></span></span>. Unsigned overflow is the carry out of the top bit. A classic sensor bug: reading a 16-bit two’s-complement accelerometer register as unsigned turns −1 into 65 535.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"bits\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Toggle the bits of an 8-bit register and read it as unsigned and as two’s complement. Negate flips every bit and adds one.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>An IMU’s 16-bit temperature register reads <code>0xFF38</code>, and the datasheet says temperature = raw/256 + 25 °C.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Unsigned: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">xFF</span></span><span class=\"mord\">38</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">65</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">336</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>The MSB is set, so as two’s complement: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">65</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">336</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">65</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">536</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">200</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Temperature: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">200/256</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">25</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">24.22</span></span></span></span> °C. Read as unsigned, it would claim 280 °C.</li>\n<li>Check by negating: invert 0xFF38 to get 0x00C7 = 199, add 1 to get 200. So the raw value is −200. ✓</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">twos.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">encode</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">v, bits</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Signed integer -&gt; unsigned bit pattern; raises on overflow.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    lo, hi = -(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; (bits - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)), (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; (bits - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> lo &lt;= v &lt;= hi:\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">raise</span> OverflowError(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{v}</span> doesn&#x27;t fit in <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{bits}</span> bits&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> v &amp; ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; bits) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">decode</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">u, bits</span>):\n    u &amp;= (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; bits) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> u - (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; bits) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> u &gt;&gt; (bits - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> u\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">add_signed</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b, bits</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Returns (result, overflow) the way an ALU would.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    s = (encode(a, bits) + encode(b, bits)) &amp; ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; bits) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n    r = decode(s, bits)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> r, (a &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>) == (b &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> (r &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>) != (a &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">negate</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">u, bits</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> ((~u) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) &amp; ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; bits) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> v <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">32768</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">32768</span>):                         <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># every 16-bit value round-trips</span>\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> decode(encode(v, <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>) == v\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> decode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFF38</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>) == -<span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(decode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFF38</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">25</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">24.21875</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> negate(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFF38</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> decode(negate(encode(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">128</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>) == -<span class=\"hljs-number\">128</span>   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># -128 has no positive twin</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> add_signed(<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>) == (-<span class=\"hljs-number\">56</span>, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> add_signed(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>) == (-<span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> add_signed(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">128</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>) == (<span class=\"hljs-number\">127</span>, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> encode(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFD</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> encode(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFD</span>                            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># sign extension</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> v <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">128</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">129</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">try</span>:\n            encode(v, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">raise</span> AssertionError(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;no overflow detected&quot;</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">except</span> OverflowError:\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">pass</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> decode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0x80000000</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">32</span>) == -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>**<span class=\"hljs-number\">31</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;all 65536 values round-trip; overflow rules check out&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Write −1, −128 and +127 as 8-bit hex.</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>0xFF, 0x80, 0x7F.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A 12-bit ADC in differential mode returns two’s complement in the low 12 bits of a 16-bit register: 0x0F9C. What signed value is it?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Low 12 bits 0xF9C = 3996. Bit 11 is set, so the value is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3996</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4096</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">100</span></span></span></span>. Sign-extend before using it: 0xFF9C as 16 bits.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p06-l01\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"positional-notation","title":"Positional notation"},{"id":"two-s-complement","title":"Two’s complement"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p06-l01-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>What is 0xB5 in decimal?</p>\n","explain":"<p>11×16 + 5.</p>\n","answer":181,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l01-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>What signed value does the 16-bit pattern 0xFF38 hold?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Subtract <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">16</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> because the MSB is set.</p>\n","answer":-200,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l01-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Two’s-complement negation is…</p>\n","explain":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7477em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n","options":["flip the MSB","invert every bit and add 1","subtract 1 and invert the MSB","reverse the bit order"],"answer":1},{"id":"p06-l01-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>What is the smallest 16-bit signed value?</p>\n","explain":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n","answer":-32768,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l01-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Signed addition overflows when…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The carry out is the unsigned overflow rule.</p>\n","options":["there is a carry out of the top bit","both operands have the same sign and the result’s sign differs","the result is zero","one operand is negative"],"answer":1},{"id":"p06-l01-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>The 12-bit two’s-complement value 0xF9C, in decimal?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Bit 11 is set.</p>\n","answer":-100,"tol":0.001,"unit":""}],"code":[{"file":"twos.py","lang":"python","src":"def encode(v, bits):\n    \"\"\"Signed integer -> unsigned bit pattern; raises on overflow.\"\"\"\n    lo, hi = -(1 << (bits - 1)), (1 << (bits - 1)) - 1\n    if not lo <= v <= hi:\n        raise OverflowError(f\"{v} doesn't fit in {bits} bits\")\n    return v & ((1 << bits) - 1)\n\ndef decode(u, bits):\n    u &= (1 << bits) - 1\n    return u - (1 << bits) if u >> (bits - 1) else u\n\ndef add_signed(a, b, bits):\n    \"\"\"Returns (result, overflow) the way an ALU would.\"\"\"\n    s = (encode(a, bits) + encode(b, bits)) & ((1 << bits) - 1)\n    r = decode(s, bits)\n    return r, (a >= 0) == (b >= 0) and (r >= 0) != (a >= 0)\n\ndef negate(u, bits):\n    return ((~u) + 1) & ((1 << bits) - 1)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    for v in range(-32768, 32768):                         # every 16-bit value round-trips\n        assert decode(encode(v, 16), 16) == v\n    assert decode(0xFF38, 16) == -200 and abs(decode(0xFF38, 16) / 256 + 25 - 24.21875) < 1e-12\n    assert negate(0xFF38, 16) == 200 and decode(negate(encode(-128, 8), 8), 8) == -128   # -128 has no positive twin\n    assert add_signed(100, 100, 8) == (-56, True) and add_signed(-100, 50, 8) == (-50, False)\n    assert add_signed(-128, -1, 8) == (127, True)\n    assert encode(-3, 8) == 0xFD and encode(-3, 16) == 0xFFFD                            # sign extension\n    for v in (128, -129):\n        try:\n            encode(v, 8); raise AssertionError(\"no overflow detected\")\n        except OverflowError:\n            pass\n    assert decode(0x80000000, 32) == -2**31\n    print(\"all 65536 values round-trip; overflow rules check out\")"}]}